10.3 Multiple-point calibration involves the measurement of absorbed power over a large range of power settings. Typically, for a 600 W unit, the following power settings are measured: 100, 99, 98, 97, 95, 90, 80, 70, 60, 50, and 40% using the procedure described in Sec. 10.5. These data are clustered about the customary working power ranges. Non-linearity has been encountered at the upper end of the calibration.
Non-linearity is primarily encountered when using older instrumentation, however, multipoint calibration is recommended for use with all instrumentation when accurate and precise temperature feedback control is not available
